    {
     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p16-information-block",
     "replacement": "- **Scientific notation**, also called **standard form**, writes a number as $a\\times10^n$, where $1\\le a<10$ and $n$ is an integer.\n- The number $a$ is the **coefficient** and $10^n$ is a **power of 10**.\n- It is used to write very large or very small numbers.",
