    {
     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p18-method",
     "replacement": "1. Place a decimal point after the first non-zero digit.\n2. Count the places the decimal point moved. This is the size of the exponent $n$.\n3. Write the number as $a\\times10^n$:\n  a. $n$ is positive when the number is at least 10 (the decimal point moved left),\n  b. $n$ is negative when the number is between 0 and 1 (the decimal point moved right).\n  If the decimal point does not move, $n=0$.",
