     "replacement": "For $a\\times10^n$\n\n1. Move the decimal point left or right depending on the sign of $n$. Fill any empty places with zeros.\n  - If $n$ is positive, move the decimal point $n$ places to the right.\n  - If $n$ is negative, move the decimal point $|n|$ places to the left.\n\n**Remember:** in scientific notation, numbers that are at least 10 have positive exponents, numbers between 0 and 1 have negative exponents, and numbers from 1 up to 10 have exponent 0.",
     "autoApply": true,
