     "op": "theory",
     "blockId": "p9-significant-figures-information",
     "replacement": "- **Significant figures** are the meaningful digits in a number.\n- Timber cannot be cut to a length of $1.333\\,333\\ldots\\ \\mathrm{m}$.\n- Digits beyond a certain place are meaningless.\n- **Rules for significant figures:**\n  1. The first significant figure is the first non-zero digit (reading from left to right). Zeros before it are not significant.\n  2. All non-zero digits are significant.\n  3. Zeros between non-zero digits are significant.\n  4. Zeros after the last non-zero digit of a decimal are significant.\n  5. Zeros at the end of a whole number _may_ be significant.\n    Until we learn scientific notation, treat them as significant.",
     "autoApply": true,
